          "From the beginning, Login.gov has treated privacy as a core design principle. Its privacy protections are built into the service’s architecture, governance, and operating model, empowering people to access government services without their information being used for commercial purposes. This approach distinguishes Login.gov as a government-run digital identity service designed to protect the public while enabling agencies to provide secure access.",
          "Building on that foundation, recent developments include enhancing established anti-fraud capabilities, lowering pricing for agency partners, and starting a new design collaboration focused on improving the user experience. Together, these efforts enable a more secure, accessible, and consistent way for the public to access digital government services.",
